{
    "name": "host_toolchain",
    "role": "the host C++ toolchain every FSLA workspace that compiles C++ registers (the environment extension's `host_toolchain` tag), and nvcc's host compiler (`-ccbin`): PyTorch's own -- the gcc-toolset of its manylinux_2_28 builder for CUDA 13 (`pytorch/manylinux2_28-builder:cuda13.*`, .ci/docker/manywheel/build.sh's `DEVTOOLSET_VERSION=13`) on that builder's base, AlmaLinux 8 (glibc 2.28, the floor torch's wheels need) -- the toolset and the sysroot only, never the image: the AlmaLinux 8.10 RPMs below, each by its repository's digest, unpacked into one root. The toolset's libstdc++ links the system's libstdc++.so.6 (GCC 8's, GLIBCXX_3.4.25) and the newer symbols from libstdc++_nonshared.a, so what it links loads beside torch on any glibc >= 2.28.",
    "upstream": "https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/5baab687f6f6ade4649eb9b07ad7c8ccf1898366/.ci/docker/manywheel/build.sh (manylinux2_28-builder:cuda13*: GPU_IMAGE=amd64/almalinux:8, DEVTOOLSET_VERSION=13); .ci/docker/manywheel/Dockerfile_2_28 (gcc-toolset-${DEVTOOLSET_VERSION}-gcc, -gcc-c++)",
